/E (Fixed-Rate Mortgages: Your interest rate stays the same for the entire life of the loan. This gives you predictable payments and protection from rising interest rates, making it easier to budget. Keep in mind that shorter loan terms \(like 15 years\) usually have lower rates but higher monthly payments compared to a 30-year loan.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
